{
  "doc": "PROFILE.md §6.2: '`ClassFlags` splits into `Synthetic`, `KeyPoint`, `Withheld` and `Overlap`.' Splitting one packed byte into four dimensions must not change the values it carried: `tiny14.las` was written with every class-flag bit clear, so each of the four dimensions reads 0 for all 25 points. The four are reported by pdal info.rst's '--stats  Dump stats on all points', restricted with '--dimensions' to one dimension per invocation so that each run's single `stats.statistic` entry is the dimension named on its own command line -- nothing here depends on the order in which an implementation registers or reports the four.",
